<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 64,170 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 64,170 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 64,170 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday, compared to 72,908 tonnes on in the previous 24 hours.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>					    Wednesday	Previous</p>
<p>    Export cargo			14,227	    8,578</p>
<p>    Import cargo			49,943	   64,330</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, five ships sailed and eight berthed. In the next 24 hours, six ships were expected to sail and six were expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at the Karachi Port:</p>
<p>Commodity		Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		  Berthing</p>
<p>High speed deisel    35,000	 Al-Sabiyah	   due</p>
<p>Gas oil		  27,000	 Nike		 24/11</p>
<p>Palm oil		 13,500	 Wawasan Courage  29/11</p>
<p>Gas oil		  40,000	 Ying Song Hu	 due</p>
<p>Palm oil		  5,000	 Helena	     26/11</p>
<p>Crude oil		65,000	 Capitan Mirinda  26/11</p>
<p>high speed deisel    52,000	 Al-Maqwa	   28/11</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
